y::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\\\",\\n    \\\"exit\\\": 2\\n  },\\n  \\\"tokens\\\": {\\n    \\\"input\\\": 5419270,\\n    \\\"output\\\": 34873\\n  },\\n  \\\"cost_usd\\\": 1.9786878000000003,\\n  \\\"wall_clock_s\\\": 939.518,\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n  \\\"refusal\\\": null,\\n  \\\"halted\\\": null,\\n  \\\"stop\\\": {\\n    \\\"class\\\": \\\"unclassed\\\",\\n    \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"product\\\",\\n    \\\"detail\\\": \\\"4 deselected, 4 errors in 0.11s\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"record_version\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"item\\\": \\\"106\\\",\\n  \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"v0.17.1-8-ge72112f\\\",\\n  \\\"product_pin\\\": \\\"v0.17.1\\\"\\n}\\n## Problem\\n\\nTwo facts on the attestation of tenant zero's item #665 (merged `6ac6021`) are wrong or unreadable, and both are the product's. First, the two record commits `attavo drive` made (`e7d9860`, `f572d73`) are authored and committed as the operator's own git identity, because `commit_record` calls `git commit --only` with no identity while `executor_identity` already sets one for the executor's commits; a read by author cannot tell a driver's transport commit from a person's, so the driven clause of Phase 3 is provable only from the attestation's `acts` and not from the log. Second, the attestation carries `ci_runs: 0` on an item whose three pushes each ran six checks: the field is `int(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_CI_RUNS\\\") or 0)`, set by no template, so it reports a wrong number rather than none.\\n\\nThis item gives the driver its own identity and removes `ci_runs`. `commit_record` authors and commits every record commit as `attavo driver <driver@attavo.invalid>` from a `driver_identity()` beside `executor_identity()`, set by the product and never the tenant's git config, so `git log --author='attavo driver'` on a driven item lists exactly the driver's transport commits; the executor's identity is unchanged. A test in `tests/test_drive.py` sets the fixture tenant's `user.name` to another value, drives to a record commit, and asserts author and committer name and email on it; it must fail against the current `commit_record`. `ci_runs` leaves the attestation statement, the schema's `required` list and `properties`, and `ATTAVO_CI_RUNS` is read nowhere; `tests/test_attest.py::test_partial_does_not_read_ci_runs` is retired with it, and a test asserts the statement `attavo attest` prints carries no `ci_runs` key. The attestation schema's `$id` moves from `/attestation/v1` to `/attestation/v2`, since a required field left the shape. No other behaviour changes; a forge-read producer for CI runs is Phase 4's, if a decision ever needs the number.\\n\\nRetires: the by-author read as something the attestation's `acts` field had to stand in for; `ATTAVO_CI_RUNS` and the test that guarded it; one wrong number on every attestation.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- bin/attavo\\n- schema/attestation.schema.json\\n- tests/test_drive.py\\n- tests/test_attest.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- no-ci-runs.sh: neither bin/attavo nor the attestation schema mentions ci_runs or ATTAVO_CI_RUNS\\n- attestation-schema-v2.sh: the attestation schema's $id is /attestation/v2\\n- driver-identity.sh: bin/attavo declares driver_identity with the driver@attavo.invalid address\\nattest/specs/106/spec.md\\nattest/specs/106/criteria/attestation-schema-v2.sh\\nattest/specs/106/criteria/no-ci-runs.sh\\nattest/specs/106/criteria/driver-identity.sh\\nschema_version = 1\\n\\n[attavo]\\nversion = \\\"v0.17.1\\\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nchecks_command = \\\"python3 .attavo/bin/forge-checks\\\"\\nfile_issue_command = \\\"python3 .attavo/bin/file-issue\\\"\\n\\n[executor]\\nbuild = \\\"claude-code\\\"\\nverify = \\\"codex\\\"\\n\\n[executor.claude-code]\\nauth = \\\"subscription\\\"\\nmodel = \\\"claude-sonnet-5\\\"\\n\\n[executor.codex]\\nmodel = \\\"gpt-5.6-sol\\\"\\n\\n[spec]\\n[spec.boundary]\\npaths = [\\\"bin/**\\\", \\\"adapters/**\\\", \\\"schema/**\\\", \\\"templates/**\\\", \\\"action.yml\\\", \\\"scripts/**\\\"]\\n\\n[gates]\\n[gates.spec]\\ncommand = \\\"attavo spec-gate\\\"\\nretires = [\\n  \\\"the lane as the product's transport: a Claude Code lane session reporting to a reviewing session, with no spec, no approval bound to a commit, no build/verify separation, and no attestation on the product's own commits\\\",\\n  \\\"the || true step in ci.yml that ran the doctor's four proofs against this repository expected to still fail\\\",\\n  \\\"the reviewing session as the reader of whether the lane did what the issue said\\\",\\n]\\n\\n[tests]\\nselect = \\\"python3 .attavo/bin/select-tests\\\"\\nrun = \\\"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\\\"\\n\\n[paths]\\nspecs = \\\"attest/specs\\\"\\nrecords = \\\"attest/records\\\"\\nrulings = \\\"attest/rulings.md\\\"\\nrejections = \\\"attest/rejections\\\"\\n\\n[operators]\\napprovers = [\\\"dbean10\\\"]\\n\\n[checks]\\ncommand = \\\"python3 -m pytest tests -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\\\"\\ndiff --git a/attest/records/106/approval-01.json b/attest/records/106/approval-01.json\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..3c62a68\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/records/106/approval-01.json\\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\\n+{\\n+  \\\"sha\\\": \\\"f51bbf93410c24fcc4b6026f60b6a3f84a5c315a\\\",\\n+  \\\"spec_sha\\\": \\\"dbff340f33d8f21c1d200f0b1dbb0f7d7788e22b\\\",\\n+  \\\"approved_by\\\": \\\"dbean10\\\",\\n+  \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-09-13T15:38:17Z\\\",\\n+  \\\"record_version\\\": 2,\\n+  \\\"item\\\": \\\"106\\\",\\n+  \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"v0.17.1\\\",\\n+  \\\"product_pin\\\": \\\"v0.17.1\\\"\\n+}\\ndiff --git a/attest/records/106/spec-01.json b/attest/records/106/spec-01.json\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..607741e\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/records/106/spec-01.json\\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\\n+{\\n+  \\\"sha\\\": \\\"dbff340f33d8f21c1d200f0b1dbb0f7d7788e22b\\\",\\n+  \\\"spec_sha\\\": \\\"dbff340f33d8f21c1d200f0b1dbb0f7d7788e22b\\\",\\n+  \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-09-13T09:06:34Z\\\",\\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\",\\n+  \\\"approval_sha\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n+    {\\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"no-ci-runs.sh\\\",\\n+      \\\"on_tree\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\"on_stub\\\": 0\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"attestation-schema-v2.sh\\\",\\n+      \\\"on_tree\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\"on_stub\\\": 0\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"driver-identity.sh\\\",\\n+      \\\"on_tree\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\"on_stub\\\": 0\\n+    }\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\"refusal\\\": null,\\n+  \\\"record_version\\\": 2,\\n+  \\\"item\\\": \\\"106\\\",\\n+  \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"v0.17.1\\\",\\n+  \\\"product_pin\\\": \\\"v0.17.1\\\"\\n+}\\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/106/criteria/attestation-schema-v2.sh b/attest/specs/106/criteria/attestation-schema-v2.sh\\nnew file mode 100755\\nindex 0000000..aa108f8\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/specs/106/criteria/attestation-schema-v2.sh\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+#!/bin/sh\\n+grep -q '\\\"$id\\\": \\\"https://attavo.dev/attestation/v2\\\"' schema/attestation.schema.json\\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/106/criteria/driver-identity.sh b/attest/specs/106/criteria/driver-identity.sh\\nnew file mode 100755\\nindex 0000000..c6dee9d\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/specs/106/criteria/driver-identity.sh\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+#!/bin/sh\\n+grep -q 'def driver_identity' bin/attavo && grep -q 'driver@attavo.invalid' bin/attavo\\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/106/criteria/no-ci-runs.sh b/attest/specs/106/criteria/no-ci-runs.sh\\nnew file mode 100755\\nindex 0000000..5830a7b\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/specs/106/criteria/no-ci-runs.sh\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+#!/bin/sh\\n+! grep -n 'ci_runs\\\\|ATTAVO_CI_RUNS' bin/attavo schema/attestation.schema.json\\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/106/spec.md b/attest/specs/106/spec.md\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..b1759de\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/specs/106/spec.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\\n+## Problem\\n+\\n+Two facts on the attestation of tenant zero's item #665 (merged `6ac6021`) are wrong or unreadable, and both are the product's. First, the two record commits `attavo drive` made (`e7d9860`, `f572d73`) are authored and committed as the operator's own git identity, because `commit_record` calls `git commit --only` with no identity while `executor_identity` already sets one for the executor's commits; a read by author cannot tell a driver's transport commit from a person's, so the driven clause of Phase 3 is provable only from the attestation's `acts` and not from the log. Second, the attestation carries `ci_runs: 0` on an item whose three pushes each ran six checks: the field is `int(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_CI_RUNS\\\") or 0)`, set by no template, so it reports a wrong number rather than none.\\n+\\n+This item gives the driver its own identity and removes `ci_runs`. `commit_record` authors and commits every record commit as `attavo driver <driver@attavo.invalid>` from a `driver_identity()` beside `executor_identity()`, set by the product and never the tenant's git config, so `git log --author='attavo driver'` on a driven item lists exactly the driver's transport commits; the executor's identity is unchanged. A test in `tests/test_drive.py` sets the fixture tenant's `user.name` to another value, drives to a record commit, and asserts author and committer name and email on it; it must fail against the current `commit_record`. `ci_runs` leaves the attestation statement, the schema's `required` list and `properties`, and `ATTAVO_CI_RUNS` is read nowhere; `tests/test_attest.py::test_partial_does_not_read_ci_runs` is retired with it, and a test asserts the statement `attavo attest` prints carries no `ci_runs` key. The attestation schema's `$id` moves from `/attestation/v1` to `/attestation/v2`, since a required field left the shape. No other behaviour changes; a forge-read producer for CI runs is Phase 4's, if a decision ever needs the number.\\n+\\n+Retires: the by-author read as something the attestation's `acts` field had to stand in for; `ATTAVO_CI_RUNS` and the test that guarded it; one wrong number on every attestation.\\n+\\n+## Claims\\n+\\n+- bin/attavo\\n+- schema/attestation.schema.json\\n+- tests/test_drive.py\\n+- tests/test_attest.py\\n+\\n+## Criteria\\n+\\n+- no-ci-runs.sh: neither bin/attavo nor the attestation schema mentions ci_runs or ATTAVO_CI_RUNS\\n+- attestation-schema-v2.sh: the attestation schema's $id is /attestation/v2\\n+- driver-identity.sh: bin/attavo declares driver_identity with the driver@attavo.invalid address\\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/106/stub/bin/attavo b/attest/specs/106/stub/bin/attavo\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..15eec20\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/attest/specs/106/stub/bin/attavo\\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Stub for the spec gate: proves the criteria are reachable, runs nothing.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\n+\\n+def executor_identity(adapter_name: str) -> dict:\\n+    return {\\\"name\\\": f\\\"attavo executor ({adapter_name})\\\",\\n+            \\\"email\\\": f\\\"executor+{adapter_name}@attavo.invalid\\\"}\\n+\\n+\\n+def driver_identity() -> dict:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"The driver's identity for the record commits it makes: set by the\\n+    product, never the tenant's git config, so a transport commit is never\\n+    indistinguishable from an operator's own.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+    return {\\\"name\\\": \\\"attavo driver\\\", \\\"email\\\": \\\"driver@attavo.invalid\\\"}\\ndiff --git a/at