{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,155p' .github/workflows/ci.yml && sed -n '100,145p' tests/test_coherence_template.py && git show 6c1ddbd\"'^:tests/test_drive.py >/dev/null 2>&1; git show --stat --oneline 6c1ddbd && git show --stat --oneline e91548b'","aggregated_output":"name: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n  pull_request:\n  merge_group:\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n      - run: pip install pytest jsonschema\n      - run: >\n          python3 -m pytest tests -q\n          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects\n          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage\n          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record\n          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\n\n  # Since #103, this repository is Attavo's own second tenant (attavo.toml\n  # at the root) and the doctor's four proofs run for real, not under\n  # || true. attavo doctor . fails until an item has traversed every\n  # stage (proof one-item-every-stage): this job is expected red on main\n  # until the first item merges, so it is not yet a required check --\n  # the operator makes it required once that item lands.\n  #\n  # #106: proof two (a driven item's forge is green) has no vacuous case,\n  # so this job is red on every pull request until this tenant's first\n  # item has merged. Conditioned on pushes to main only until then; a\n  # later item returns it to pull requests and merge groups.\n  doctor:\n    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n      - run: pip install pytest jsonschema\n      - name: doctor's four proofs\n        run: python3 -m pytest tests/test_doctor.py -q -k \"every_gate_rejects or one_item_traversed_every_stage or no_commit_lacks_a_record or no_stop_lacks_cause\"\n      - run: python3 bin/attavo doctor .\n\n  action-self-check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - uses: ./\n      - run: attavo spec-gate\n        working-directory: tests/fixtures/valid\n        env:\n          ATTAVO_ITEM: \"1\"\n\n  # merge_group added alongside pull_request (#103): the merge queue\n  # requires every required check to report on the merge group, not only\n  # on the pull request that entered it (tenant zero's #662 was the same\n  # class of miss, on pull_request only). github.base_ref is empty on a\n  # merge_group event; the target branch comes from\n  # github.event.merge_group.base_ref there instead.\n  schema-version:\n    if: github.event_name == 'pull_request' || github.event_name == 'merge_group'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n      - name: Resolve the target branch\n        id: base\n        run: |\n          if [ \"${{ github.event_name }}\" = \"merge_group\" ]; then\n            branch=\"${{ github.event.merge_group.base_ref }}\"\n            branch=\"${branch#refs/heads/}\"\n          else\n            branch=\"${{ github.base_ref }}\"\n          fi\n          echo \"branch=$branch\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n      - run: git fetch --no-tags origin \"${{ steps.base.outputs.branch }}\"\n      - run: python3 scripts/check_record_schema_version.py \"origin/${{ steps.base.outputs.branch }}\"\n    log, read by an operator as the check having already failed (it had\n    not: the exit code is correct and statement=false is correct).\n    2>/dev/null on the json.load line discards only that traceback -- the\n    exit code, and everything else in this file, is unchanged. Red\n    today.\"\"\"\n    script = extract_step_run(TEMPLATE.read_text(), \"attavo attest\")\n    json_load_line = next(l for l in script.splitlines() if \"json.load\" in l)\n    assert json_load_line.rstrip().endswith(\"2>/dev/null; then\")\n\n\ndef test_digest_and_signing_steps_require_the_statement_output():\n    \"\"\"The header's promise -- a not-yet or zero-item line makes the\n    captured file a non-statement the later steps skip -- must be a real\n    guard, not just true on the happy path: on the merge group of a pull\n    request carrying no item, attest exits 0 with a non-JSON line, and\n    without this guard actions/attest would be handed prose. Written and\n    run red before either step read this output.\"\"\"\n    text = TEMPLATE.read_text()\n    for name in (\"Compute the merge commit's subject digest\", \"Sign the attestation record\"):\n        block = step_block(text, f\"- name: {name}\")\n        if_line = next(l.strip() for l in block.splitlines() if l.strip().startswith(\"if:\"))\n        assert if_line == (\"if: github.event_name == 'merge_group' && \"\n                           \"steps.attest.outputs.statement == 'true'\"), name\n\n\ndef test_checkout_step_has_no_ref_and_full_history():\n    text = TEMPLATE.read_text()\n    checkout_block = step_block(text, \"- uses: actions/checkout@v4\")\n    assert \"ref:\" not in checkout_block\n    assert \"fetch-depth: 0\" in checkout_block\n\n\ndef test_predicate_type_is_the_ruled_url():\n    \"\"\"Moved from the deleted tests/test_attest_template.py (issue #54's\n    test, retired alongside the file it exercised).\"\"\"\n    assert \"predicate-type: https://attavo.dev/attestation/v1\" in TEMPLATE.read_text()\n\n\ndef test_signing_step_inputs_are_a_subset_of_actions_attest_v2_and_include_predicate_path():\n    \"\"\"Issue #70: the template once passed predicate-file, an input the\n    action has never declared, and continue-on-error swallowed the\n    resulting warning as a signing refusal. Reading the action's own\n    declared inputs (tests/fixtures/actions-attest-v2-inputs.json, the ten\n    names from that run's own warning) catches the typo class rather than\n    the one typo.\"\"\"\n    block = step_block(TEMPLATE.read_text(), \"- name: Sign the attestation record\")\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-pmuVuocT' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-JYGJqBsA' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n6c1ddbd Spec #106: the driver's own identity, and ci_runs leaves the attestation\n bin/attavo                     | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------\n schema/attestation.schema.json |  5 ++---\n tests/test_attest.py           | 20 +++++++++++---------\n tests/test_drive.py            | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-nJLeNbdu' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-ckNtbPO4' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ne91548b attavo: doctor job reports on main only until #106 merges\n .github/workflows/ci.yml | 6 ++++++\n 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"The coherence workflow still signs v2 statements as the v1 predicate type\",\"specimen\":\"templates/workflows/attavo-coherence.yml (unchanged by 6c1ddbd; lines 40 and 118 still use https://attavo.dev/attestation/v1), while schema/attestation.schema.json declares https://attavo.dev/attestation/v2\",\"retires\":\"The build’s implicit claim that changing the schema $id alone completes the attestation-v2 migration; it also closes the stale v1 predicate-type contract preserved by test_predicate_type_is_the_ruled_url.\",\"rejection_test\":\"tests/test_coherence_template.py::test_predicate_type_matches_attestation_schema_id — load schema/attestation.schema.json, read its $id, and assert the workflow’s predicate-type equals it (replacing the current test that explicitly requires /v1).\",\"severity\":\"Blocking when a schema-v2 attestation reaches the merge_group signing step: it is published under the v1 predicate type; harmless only while no v2 statement is signed through that workflow.\"}],\"tests_named\":[\"tests/test_coherence_template.py::test_predicate_type_matches_attestation_schema_id\"]}"}}
